[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_item")
id = "keld_orders"
display_name = "Brother Keld's Orders"
description = "A folded sheet in the Mercy's grey wax, and under it a tally of carts in a miner's square hand."
value = 0
weight = 0.1
quest_item = true
book_text = "To Keld, foreman of the ninth seam, from A.

The Guilds sealed the ninth because it sang. They were right to be frightened, and wrong about why. It does not sing to them.

Cut gently. Every cart of seam-stone that goes up the Deep Road under the River Compact's licence is a cart of lights going nowhere; the stone holds them like a cage holds a bird. Weirholt's mill has one. Ilunhall's cistern has a whole conduit. They will be glad of it when the time comes, and they will not know why.

When the seam is cut back to the blind ones' song, stop. Do not go down. The Choir below is not yours to harvest, and not mine. Not yet.

Bring what you have to the forest city by the next dark of the Wanderer. Ithmarren keeps its own wells, and keeps them badly.

- A.

(Below, in Keld's hand: Cart 112. Cart 113. Cart 114. The singing is louder at the face. Two of the lads won't go past the props. I don't blame them.)"
